ided to  use the results from tournaments held in  2018 and 2019  to determine who qualifies except  boujold wasn't fighting then  she was pregnant with her daughter kate  her olympic dream  she learned in an email was over do you  feel let down by the olympic movement  i do i honestly i do and it's  unfortunate i think you know being an  olympian has always been something i've  been super proud of  before getting pregnant she was the  number two fighter in the americas  as well as a quarter finalist in the rio  olympic games in 2016.  she thought the ioc had made a mistake  however she was told if they made an  exception for her  they'd have to make it for everyone the  argument that this is somehow  going to cause unfairness for everyone  else they're gonna have to if they  change the rule for this case the  floodgates will open and they'll get all  these appeals for real changes  well what floodgates how many people are  getting pregnant pujold isn't alone in  her corner  tennis icon billie jean king has  expressed support and the canadian  olympic committee and  minister of heritage have sent letters  to the ioc  but will the ioc listen earlier this  year the head of the tokyo organizing  committee was forced to resign  after making sexist comments in response  the ioc made a point of stressing its  commitment to women's issues  urging each competing country to have a  male and female flag bearer  and calling tokyo the first gender equal  olympic games the legal angle  for mandy is not a fairness issue  it's a human right violation violation  of the olympic charter issue  because of the pregnancy bujold has  filed an appeal with the court of  arbitration for sport  in boxing she's never backed away from a  fight  as a mother it's out of the question so  i'm trying to be that example for her to  show her hey when she looks back on this  you know later in life and says  wow like my mom did that right  microlight global news kitchener ontario  and what an example s